# The template trace (`:trace template`) of the shapes trace-all does not
# have: a direct call to a template of two parameters (its signature is a
# list), a template that is a variable-bound LAMBDA (it has no name, so the
# trace says `<lambda>`), and two templates of two parameters instantiated
# because a call THROUGH A VALUE reaches them (value-instantiate). And the
# final `infer` trace of a `const` container (a const scalar has no symbol).
:trace template infer on
func pair(a, b) { var t = a; return t + b; }
pair(1, 2.5)
var idl = func(x) => x * 3
idl(4)
const CA = [1, 2]
func w1(a, b) => a + b; func w2(a, b) => a - b; var wo = [w1, w2]; wo[runtime(0)](5, 3)
:trace all off
